<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-103>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-103" ;
  triage:title "v1.3-consumer compatibility fixture materially thinner than AC9's own wording" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-http-runtime/tests/http_v1_3_compat.rs only asserts major-version equality and that one pre-AZ route still resolves. It does not test 'every pre-AZ route,' does not test that a 1.3.0 client ignores additive task response fields, and does not test the sprint's own explicitly required behavior: 'New task requests sent to a 1.3.0 daemon fail with the existing typed unsupported-route/version response before mutation.' Confirmed at head 6937c547f. Fix: expand http_v1_3_compat.rs to cover all three gaps per AC9's own wording. Source: QA-1 on PR #1382 (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1382#issuecomment-5612459494)." ;
